ENTRY            32924   20260708   20261124   20261124       3224
SUBENT        32924001   20260708   20261124   20261124       3224
BIB                 13         53
TITLE      Measurement of the neutron total cross section of 9Be
            at the Back-n white neutron source of CSNS
AUTHOR     (Jiangbo Bai, Jingyu Tang, Liqun Shi, Yonghao Chen,
            Han Yi, Jie Bao, Yu Bao, Ping Cao, Haolei Chen,
            Zhen Chen, Zengqi Cui, Ruirui Fan, Changqing Feng,
            Keqing Gao, Xiaolong Gao, Minhao Gu, Changcai Han,
            Guozhu He, Yongcheng He, Yang Hong, Yiwei Hu,
            Hanxiong Huang, Xiru Huang, Haoyu Jiang, Wei Jiang,
            Zhijie Jiang, Hantao Jing, Ling Kang, Bo Li, Chao Li,
            Jiawen Li, Qiang Li, Xiao Li, Yang Li, Jie Liu,
            Shubin Liu, Ze Long, Guangyuan Luan, Changjun Ning,
            Mengchen Niu, Binbin Qi, Jie Ren, Xichao Ruan,
            Zhaohui Song, Kang Sun, Zhijia Sun, Zhixin Tan,
            Xinyi Tang, Binbin Tian, Lijiao Wang, Pengcheng Wang,
            Zhaohui Wang, Xiaoguang Wu, Xuan Wu, Likun Xie,
            Xiaoyun Yang, Li Yu, Tao Yu, Yongji Yu, Guohui Zhang,
            Linhao Zhang, Qiwei Zhang, Xianpeng Zhang,
            Yuliang Zhang, Zhiyong Zhang, Luping Zhou,
            Zhihao Zhou, Kejun Zhu)
INSTITUTE  (3CPRFUD,3CPRHST,3CPRIHP,3CPRAEP,3CPRBJG,3CPRNIX,
            3CPRUCA)
REFERENCE  (J,CPH/C,48,084001,2024)
           #doi:10.1088/1674-1137/ad4c5b
FACILITY   (SYNCH,3CPRIHP) Back-n beam line of China Spallation
            Neutron Source (CSNS)
INC-SOURCE (SPALL) The measurement was performed in the normal
            double-bunch mode with a pulse repetition rate of 25
            Hz. Each proton pulse had two bunches with a time
            interval of 410 ns and a discrepancy of less than 1%
            in intensity between them. Each Gauss type bunch had
            a pulse width of about 60 ns (FWHM).
SAMPLE     Three Be samples with a diameter of 70 mm, with
            thicknesses of 9.99, 20.00 and 29.99 mm, with mass of
            71.1472, 142.1155 and 213.2921 g, and with atomic
            density of 0.12366, 0.24701 and 0.37072 atoms/barns.
DETECTOR   (FISCH) A multi-cell fast fission ionization chamber
            with high-purity 235U and 238U.
METHOD     (TOF,TRN) The flight path distance of the two 235U
            cells and two 238U cells are 77.570, 77.588, 77.660,
            and 77.678 m.
ERR-ANALYS (DATA-ERR) The total cross section relative
            uncertainty is primarily affected by the measurement
            uncertainty of the samples and the transmission
            relative uncertainty. The relative uncertainty of
            neutron counts includes statistical and unfolded
            errors. The statistical uncertainties were obtained
            from the 1 sigma counting statistics of the data
            collected in the individual energy bins.
COMMENT    The authors recommend the results of 29.99 mm Be for
            the total cross section uncertainty was the smallest.
STATUS     (TABLE,,Jiangbo Bai+,J,CPH/C,48,084001,2024)
HISTORY    (20241014R) The data received from Jiangbo Bai
           (20260708C) Jimin WANG
ENDBIB              53
NOCOMMON             0          0
ENDSUBENT           56
SUBENT        32924002   20260708   20261124   20261124       3224
BIB                  3          3
REACTION   (4-BE-9(N,TOT),,SIG)
COMMENT    The measured results with 235U cells
STATUS     (COREL,32924003) Data measured with 238U cells
ENDBIB               3
